  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<p>Correct answer: C</p>\n<p>A: This represents the kinetic energy of only the block with mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3M\"></span>.</p>\n<p>B: This represents the kinetic energy of only the block with mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M\"></span>.</p>\n<p>C: From conservation of momentum, the initial momentum is zero. Therefore, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Mv = 3M v'\"></span>, where <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v'\"></span> is the speed of the larger block. This gives <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v' = \\frac{1}{3} v\"></span>. The total kinetic energy is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E_{k} = \\frac{1}{2} M v^{2} + \\frac{1}{2} (3M) (\\frac{v}{3})^{2} = \\frac{1}{2} M v^{2} + \\frac{1}{6} M v^{2} = \\frac{2}{3} M v^{2}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>D: This assumes both blocks move at the same speed <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span>.</p>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_1a",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Two blocks with masses <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3M\"></span> are placed on a frictionless horizontal surface. A compressed spring is held between them and then released, as shown in the diagram.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>Immediately after the blocks lose contact with the spring, the block of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M\"></span> moves to the left with a speed <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v\"></span>.</p>\n<p>What is the total kinetic energy of the two blocks?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{6} M v^{2}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2} M v^{2}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2}{3} M v^{2}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2 M v^{2}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
